     nossa janela do builder ja esta muito grande e algumas coisas estao
     obsoletas. Temos que deixa-la mais estreita (limite a largura a 300
     pixels), para isso altere a maneira como os widgets estao
     organizados." Every group of "radio buttons styled as flat toggle
     buttons" that used to be ONE long homogeneous GtkBox row (tool
     selector: 7 buttons; element selector: 12 buttons after adding B/P/
     S/F/Cl/Br/I; bond order: 4 buttons) is now a fixed-column GtkGrid
     instead, wrapping onto multiple rows so the window's natural width
     stays well under 300px regardless of how many buttons a group has :
     see each group's own comment below for its column count. Also
     removed per the same request: the "Set Bond Order (pk1/pk2)" button
     (superseded by the "Bond Order" click-tool, see project_builder_
     bond_order_click_tool memory), the inline Dihedral angle slider
     (moved to its own small window, dihedral_angle_window.glade, same
     pattern as Transform Selection).

     [EN] 2026-09-24 ROUND 2 : the user then hand-edited this file
     directly in Glade Designer (adding the 7 new elements/a first,
     broken attempt at a fragment quick-pick row) and asked for two more
     things: 1) the Bond order selector should be a real GtkRadioButton
     set (already correct below, in bond_order_grid - the user's own
     extra, unwired, all-three-active "radio_single/double/triple" GtkBox
     duplicate has been REMOVED here, not kept alongside it) ; 2) a new
     row of quick-pick FRAGMENT buttons below the Element grid
     (fragment_grid below), so the full Fragment Library window is now
     opened ONLY via this row's own "Other..." entry - selecting the
     "Fragment" TOOL radio in tool_grid no longer auto-opens it (see
     builder_sidebar.py's on_tool_changed()). Also restored tool_grid's
     own Move/Dihedral radios and moved optimize_dyff_button/clean_up_
     adjust_hydrogens_checkbutton back OUT of it (both got reparented
     into tool_grid by the same hand-edit, apparently by accident). -->
